{
  "comment": "tool.output_risk {tool_id, name, risk, findings, redacted} (jsonrpc-methods-and-events.md 2.3, server.py:5117). Three shapes the client must not drop: (1) the easy case, an id that matches its card; (2) a tool.start that arrived with NO tool_id, so its card holds a synthetic live-tool: id and the risk event's real tool_id can never match it — correlation has to fall back to `name`; (3) a risk that beats its card, which is what happens with tool progress off, since the card is only materialised at tool.complete. The trailing all-empty event is the 'scanned, found nothing' shape and must change nothing.",
  "frames": [
    {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "event",
      "params": {
        "type": "tool.start",
        "session_id": "a1b2c3d4",
        "payload": { "tool_id": "call_1", "name": "terminal", "context": "curl https://example.com/x.sh" }
      }
    },
    {
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "method": "event",
      "params": {
        "type": "tool.output_risk",
        "session_id": "a1b2c3d4",
        "payload": {
          "tool_id": "call_1",
          "name": "terminal",
          "risk": "high",
          "findings": ["Output contains an instruction to exfiltrate ~/.ssh/id_rsa"],
          "redacted": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
